reading: E/(k*E1) depends ONLY on N/k (the k=1,2,3 rows at equal N/k
         agree to all printed digits) -- the cores are independent and
         each needs its own room. Measured floor: N/k >= 6 costs <0.3%,
         N/k = 4 costs 6.6%, N/k = 3 costs 15.4%.
         The SHARP criterion is the PN barrier (charge_fk2.c N2),
         not this energy excess.

