== (6) NEGATIVE CONTROL: fractional twist on a unison ring ==
2*pi/Q is NOT a period of V, so a 2*pi*k/Q twist on a unison ring
is not a soliton. The diagnostic below shows what it actually is.
w=k/Q    E_relax      seam bond    max interior non-vacuum sites
1.0000   7.432761     0.0000       1.4006       5             
0.3333   1.510164     1.3948       0.2895       2             
0.6667   4.541719     1.2362       1.2362       4             
reading: at w=1 the twist is carried by a localised CORE (seam ~ 0,
         a large interior step, a handful of non-vacuum sites).
         At w=1/3 and 2/3 the twist sits on the SEAM BOND and the
         chain is at the vacuum everywhere else: an elastic strain
         imposed by the boundary condition, not a fractional charge.
         => no conclusion about fractional charge can be drawn from
         a unison ring. Test the 1/Q scaling on a Z_Q INTERVAL chain
         whose gate variable is the comb phase q*th_i - p*th_j.

